# gdlint configuration. Run via `make lint`.
# Only the rules that deviate from gdtoolkit's defaults are listed here;
# dump the full default set with `gdlint --dump-default-config`.

# Declaration-ordering inside a class. Disabled deliberately: it fires 27 times
# across the presentation layer (@onready vars declared beside the plain vars
# they relate to, `enum State` sitting next to the consts it indexes), and
# satisfying it means reshuffling declarations for no correctness benefit.
disable:
- class-definitions-order

# Command `validate()` methods are guard-clause validators — one early return
# per rejection reason, each with its own error string (attack_command has 9).
# That shape is required by the command pattern in CLAUDE.md; collapsing it into
# nested conditionals would be strictly worse. 12 leaves room without inviting
# sprawl.
max-returns: 12

# Ratchet, not a target, in the same spirit as max-file-lines below:
# scenes/battle/battle_view.gd is the widest class and sits at exactly 21 — it is
# the board's rendering facade, so each method is one thing the scene asks it to
# draw (a sprite, an overlay, the fog pass, the HUD). It went 20 -> 21 when
# `_restage_identity` became `restage_identity`: the scenario driver was already
# calling it across the class boundary, and a public seam is the honest spelling
# of a caller another class has. Adding to BattleView means moving something out
# first, which is the point.
#
# It went 21 -> 22 for `hud_chip_rect`, the one owner of the corner the floating
# commander chip occupied, and back down to 21 when the docked HUD bars retired
# both: there is no floating chip left for a menu to dodge, so the geometry seam
# came out with it. Adding to BattleView still means moving something out first.
#
# BattleView is down to 19 and no longer the widest class: the field overlays
# wanted a fourth painter and a fifth mark on the board, it was sitting at exactly
# 21, so the transient paint moved out to scenes/battle/battle_overlays.gd rather
# than the ceiling moving — the ratchet doing exactly the job it is for. What is
# left there is the board itself: terrain, sprites, fog, the two HUD bars, the
# forecast.
#
# The number stays at 21 because it now binds core/game_state.gd and the two
# save-codec suites, which sit there. It is a repo-wide ceiling, so it only comes
# down when the widest class does — and lowering it to BattleView's new count would
# fail three files that have not changed.
#
# 21 -> 22 for the same reason max-file-lines went to 918, to 940 and to 1420:
# merging landed two independent additions in one class at once. The audit gave
# BattleView `set_ai_teams` and `unit_order_line` — the scenario driver was
# reaching across the class boundary for both — while R's rest-state fire ring
# gave it `refresh_range_lens` on main, the sibling of `refresh_threat_lens` that
# lights the top bar's new chip. Neither side is loose and neither is the other's
# to trim. Adding to BattleView still means moving something out first.
#
# core/commander_type.gd carries the one per-file ignore: it is the doctrine
# hook contract, so its public count is the roster of rule seams twelve
# subclasses override, and splitting it would mean the mirror hook tree the
# commander plan's D1 rejects. It crossed the ceiling at 23 when the AI-advice
# hooks landed (stand_value, build_bias, retreat_hp_delta). The ceiling itself
# does not move, so every facade-shaped class is still held to 21.
max-public-methods: 22

